      "publisherHost": "polskabibliotekamuzyczna.pl",
      "status": 200,
      "contentType": "text/html",
      "bytesRead": 163812,
      "sha256": "5fd903bc4a880b8688b31a6efc70a07a324f9523a074d2c12909a0055f508cf3",
      "verificationMethod": "direct-http-body-capture+reviewed-excerpt",
      "excerpt": "Balakirev Mily Alexeyevich, *2 January 1837 (21 December 1836) Nizhny Novgorod (present-day Gorky), †29 (16) May 1910 Saint Petersburg, Russian composer, pianist, conductor and music activist. In 1862, together with G. Lomakin, he founded the Free Music School in St Petersburg, which he directed until 1872. Until the end of the 1860s, Balakirev served as the leader of this group, shaping its creative ideology and influencing their approach to musical folklore.",
      "excerptSha256": "7aeb382ff6f9f36084848c198aaae7cc73d4d1036dac6022cc27b22ecae8f4a5"
    },
    {
      "id": "balakirev-naxos",
      "url": "https://www.chandos.net/chanimages/Booklets/CH241-29.pdf",
      "publisher": "Chandos Records",
      "publisherHost": "www.chandos.net",
      "status": 200,
      "contentType": "application/pdf",
      "bytesRead": 2704271,
      "sha256": "f4fb2541c56d0026c8668f25216de3053eafc2bafc18da558be60c7b0899515e",
      "verificationMethod": "direct-http-body-capture+reviewed-excerpt",
      "excerpt": "Mily Alexeyevich Balakirev was an important figure in Russian music of the nineteenth century. He was born in Nizhniy Novgorod on 21 December 1836 / 2 January 1837 (the first date corresponds to the old Russian calendar).",
      "excerptSha256": "be03d6665b2a2172e8038d962657a1bbf348e4492df5af7c53d1e6e9dc661264"
    },
    {
