      "verificationMethod": "direct-http-body-capture+reviewed-excerpt",
      "excerpt": "Balakirev Milij (rus. Милий Балакирев) 1837 01 02 Žemutinis Naugardas 1910 05 29 Sankt Peterburgas, rusų kompozitorius, pianistas, dirigentas. 1862 su dirigentu G. Lomakinu įkūrė Nemokamą muzikos mokyklą.",
      "excerptSha256": "fb261ce11f78bd1ac1f8fb678e1086833a84867ad3196da7292b5203fe128cf1"
    },
    {
      "id": "roger-cmhof",
      "url": "https://countrymusichalloffame.org/hall-of-fame/roger-miller",
      "publisher": "Country Music Hall of Fame and Museum",
      "publisherHost": "countrymusichalloffame.org",
      "status": 200,
      "contentType": "text/html",
      "bytesRead": 122476,
      "sha256": "d78c6fa96815f64dc00585cc5b92034164529882f1008de212e10b353d32cb52",
      "verificationMethod": "direct-http-body-capture+reviewed-excerpt",
      "excerpt": "Born January 2, 1936 Died October 25, 1992 Birthplace Fort Worth, Texas. The most famous was “King of the Road,” a million-seller. In 1965–66 he won eleven Grammy awards. Two decades later, he received a 1985 Tony award for his score for Big River, a Broadway musical based on Mark Twain’s The Adventures of Huckleberry Finn.",
      "excerptSha256": "ee809f8d6f14d79546bf5371ebeea0ae47d4b60bf1ea9360988446671450894d"
    },
    {
      "id": "roger-tsha",
      "url": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/miller-roger-dean",
      "publisher": "Texas State Historical Association",
      "publisherHost": "www.tshaonline.org",
      "status": 200,
      "contentType": "text/html",
      "bytesRead": 137619,
      "sha256": "eb69698bf6888fb7e073eb8b6fb9b8524d25c13888345c262357a7c12eff4aed",
      "verificationMethod": "direct-http-body-capture+reviewed-excerpt",
      "excerpt": "Roger Miller, musician, composer, and television star, was born in Fort Worth, Texas, on January 2, 1936. The most famous was “King of the Road,” a million-seller. In 1985 he received five Tony awards for his score to Big River, a musical based on Huckleberry Finn. He died in Los Angeles on October 25, 1992.",
      "excerptSha256": "8687c87eb5c97568837602c9029864f7a4d70e090c1a217f5afca1e4cf0477af"
    },
    {
      "id": "roger-nashville",
      "url": "https://nashvillesongwritersfoundation.com/Site/inductee?entry_id=3863",
      "publisher": "Nashville Songwriters Hall of Fame",
      "publisherHost": "nashvillesongwritersfoundation.com",
      "status": 200,
      "contentType": "text/html",
      "bytesRead": 180573,
      "sha256": "0542778a0289c010a6e23fb13664dbca1f81c2dd7d9b798544dd53f8d8a42f76",
      "verificationMethod": "direct-http-body-capture+reviewed-excerpt",
      "excerpt": "Birth Name: Roger Dean Miller Birth Date: 01-02-1936. When “Dang Me” went #1 country, it started a three-year golden period that included his signature hit “King of the Road,” 11 Grammy Awards and his own NBC-TV series. Miller came back strong in 1985, writing the score to the Tony Award-winning hit Broadway musical Big River.",
      "excerptSha256": "5030c2fdf1dd8cb7cb524ce56566b03acf772796a321a9d7300eafa3985e7d45"
    },
    {
      "id": "todd-encyclopedia",
      "url": "https://www.encyclopedia.com/arts/educational-magazines/haynes-todd-1961",
      "publisher": "Encyclopedia.com (Gale)",
      "publisherHost": "www.encyclopedia.com",
      "status": 200,
      "contentType": "text/html",
      "bytesRead": 60033,
      "sha256": "95d9816b4e0edda03f8607a7e4fdec6cd5f22d97f71566ad48d61df876611a1d",
      "verificationMethod": "direct-http-body-capture+reviewed-excerpt",
      "excerpt": "HAYNES, Todd 1961- PERSONAL: Born January 2, 1961, in Los Angeles, CA. CAREER: Screenwriter, producer, director, actor. He cofounded Apparatus Productions, New York, 1987-91.",
      "excerptSha256": "b3fc0f72703d25608e211b70a0e8e037a91230c2cbb9f64286368001500ddf23"
    },
    {
      "id": "todd-golden",
      "url": "https://goldenglobes.com/person/todd-haynes/",
      "publisher": "Golden Globes",
      "publisherHost": "goldenglobes.com",
      "status": 200,
      "contentType": "text/html",
      "bytesRead": 72458,
      "sha256": "c615ca21ab7e4ea3ffc2a3a349d20e08530536c913c451c52240d0d03c6163b1",
      "verificationMethod": "direct-http-body-capture+reviewed-excerpt",
      "excerpt": "Todd Haynes (born January 2, 1961, in Los Angeles, California) wrote and directed Poison (1991), Safe (1995) with Julianne Moore, Velvet Goldmine (1998), Far From Heaven (2002) with Julianne Moore and Dennis Quaid, I’m Not There (2007) about Bob Dylan.",
      "excerptSha256": "6bcb16c0b592f42c1fdb12e9f19561109cff19e66c00cab4798d2e082c57427a"
    },
    {
      "id": "todd-bfi",
      "url": "https://www.bfi.org.uk/features/where-begin-todd-haynes",
      "publisher": "British Film Institute",
      "publisherHost": "www.bfi.org.uk",
      "status": 200,
      "contentType": "text/html",
      "bytesRead": 206221,
      "sha256": "f4cb1eaa3305763b9c2760f88edd69c5f84463f983af204cc16e7b5a2e2980f6",
      "verificationMethod": "direct-http-body-capture+reviewed-excerpt",
      "excerpt": "Best known as a pioneer of the New Queer Cinema movement that emerged in the late 1980s and early 1990s, Haynes foregrounds sexualities that are transgressive, deviant and disruptive. Far from Heaven (2002) was Haynes’s breakout hit, winning him his first Oscar nomination, for best original screenplay.",
      "excerptSha256": "63d496022956f27538787606df3e0259b1b1b95063923ceb7aed50e60e7c0ca6"
    },
